    bottomLine: "The model for what a belt listing should look like: model, serial, seam and surface. For owners of the named Horizon machines, or as a template for finding SportSmith’s listing for yours.",
    description: "SportSmith sells running belts for a long list of home and light-commercial treadmills, each one listed against a specific model and, usually, a serial number. This one is for the Horizon T90 with serial TM617, and the listing adds that it also fits the Horizon T100 with serial TM629C. That serial detail is what makes it our top example: makers change belts during a model's production run, and a listing tied to a serial prefix is much less likely to send you the wrong size. The listing describes a non-directional finger-splice seam, a black diamond PVC walking surface and impregnated lubrication. It was about $99 on Amazon on 6 November 2026. What it does not give is the belt's width and loop length, so measure your old belt and ask the seller to confirm both before ordering. If you own a different machine, search SportSmith's listings with your model and serial number; on the day we looked, the same format covered other Horizon, Merit, Triumph, ProForm and Sportcraft models.",
  },
  {
    id: "icon-416827",
    name: "ICON Fitness Treadmill Running Belt Part 416827 (ProForm Carbon T10)",
    brand: "ICON Fitness",
    category: "Original-equipment belt for an ICON-built treadmill",
    badge: "Best OEM Part",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=ICON+Fitness+Treadmill+Running+Belt+416827&tag=sktiger-20",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: null,
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $132 (Amazon, 6 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":132,"high":132},
    specs: "Part 416827 · ProForm Carbon T10, models 233800 and PFTL99720 · polyester belt",
    pros: [
      "Sold under the maker’s own part number by ICON, which builds ProForm and NordicTrack treadmills",
