      "The listing does not state width, loop length, seam type or warranty",
      "Listing copy is generic marketing text and mentions walking pads, which can confuse",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For a ProForm Carbon T10 owner who wants the original part; for other ICON machines, search by your belt’s part number in the same way.",
    description: "ICON Health & Fitness builds NordicTrack, ProForm and several other brands, and some of its replacement parts are sold on Amazon under the ICON Fitness name. This listing is for running belt part 416827 and names the ProForm Carbon T10 with model numbers 233800 and PFTL99720. Buying the original part number is the simplest way to avoid a size mismatch, provided your model number matches exactly. The listing describes a polyester belt and offers to help identify the right part from your model and serial number, which is worth using. It was about $132 on Amazon on 6 November 2026. The weaknesses are in the listing rather than the part: it gives no width, loop length, seam type or warranty, and its marketing copy talks about desk treadmills and walking pads, which this belt is not for. If you own a different ICON machine, find your running belt's part number in your manual's parts list or from ICON's support, and search for that number rather than the model name.",
  },
  {
    id: "sportsmith-landice-l7",
    name: "SportSmith Treadmill Pre-Lubricated Walking Belt fits 20\" x 114\" Landice L7 Treadmills",
    brand: "SportSmith",
    category: "Size-stated belt for a premium treadmill",
    badge: "Best for Premium Machines",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=SportSmith+Walking+Belt+Landice+L7+20+x+114&tag=sktiger-20",
