      "Covers a premium machine whose parts are not always easy to find",
    ],
    cons: [
      "The listing marks the fit with an asterisk; Landice L7 belts vary, so confirm your size",
      "No warranty term in the listing bullets",
      "At about $149, the most expensive belt on this page",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For a Landice L7 whose old belt measures 20 by 114 inches. The stated size is what makes it checkable.",
    description: "The Landice L7 is a premium home treadmill, and finding a running belt for one can take more work than for a mass-market machine. This SportSmith listing states the size in its title, 20 by 114 inches, which is the most useful single fact a belt listing can give: you can measure your old belt's width and loop length and know before you order whether it matches. The listing also describes a non-directional finger-splice seam, a black diamond PVC walking surface and impregnated lubrication. It was about $149 on Amazon on 6 November 2026. Note the asterisk the seller puts after the model name, which in SportSmith's listings signals that not every unit of that model uses the same belt; the stated size, not the model name, is what to match. The listing does not state a warranty, so ask before ordering. On a machine of this price, also check whether Landice or an authorised dealer can supply the original part, and compare.",
