    bottomLine: "For a NordicTrack T 6.5 S or Si whose old belt measures 127.56 by 20 inches, at about half the price of the alternatives.",
    description: "The NordicTrack T 6.5 S has been a common home treadmill for years, and belts for it are sold by several parts sellers. This one stands out on two counts: the price, about $55 on Amazon on 6 November 2026, and the detail. The listing gives the loop length, width and thickness, 127.56 by 20 by 0.08 inches, and the same figures in centimetres, which means you can check it against your old belt before you order rather than trusting the model name. It describes a rubber composite belt with a textured surface, an anti-static bottom layer and a 45 degree bevelled joint, which the seller says runs more quietly than a flat joint. We have not tested that. What the listing does not say is whether the belt is pre-lubricated, whether the joint is directional, or what warranty applies, so ask before ordering and check the underside for a direction arrow when it arrives. If your measurements match, it is the cheapest way back to a working machine on this page.",
  },
  {
    id: "walkingbelts-true-500",
    name: "WALKINGBELTS True Treadmill Running Belt Model 500 20\"",
    brand: "WALKINGBELTS",
    category: "One-ply residential belt with a long warranty",
    badge: "Longest Warranty",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=WALKINGBELTS+True+Treadmill+Running+Belt+Model+500&tag=sktiger-20",
