      "Gives width but not loop length; measure and confirm before ordering",
      "Only for True’s Model 500; other True models use different belts",
      "Seam type is not stated",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For a True Model 500 owner who wants a long warranty and a one-ply belt matched to a residential motor.",
    description: "True Fitness treadmills are built to last, which means many are still running long after their first belt has worn out. This WALKINGBELTS listing is for the True Model 500 and gives a 20 inch width. It is the only listing on this page to offer a limited lifetime warranty, and it includes the fasteners in the bundle and states that the belt is pre-lubricated with 100 percent silicone and made in the USA. The seller makes a point of the belt being one-ply, arguing that a heavier two-ply belt can overload the motor on a residential treadmill. The principle is reasonable, and matching the original construction is the safe choice, but it is the seller's argument rather than a test. The belt was about $140 on Amazon on 6 November 2026. The listing does not give the loop length or seam type, so measure your old belt and confirm both with the seller. Treat the warranty as a reason to keep the receipt and photographs of the fitted belt, not as a substitute for checking the size.",
