        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3 mb-6 flex-wrap">
          <span class="bg-[#FF5A1F] text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Buying Guide
          </span>
          <span class="bg-green-500 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Updated November 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Best Treadmill Replacement Belts <span class="text-[#5AA9FF]">and How to Match One</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          There is no such thing as a universal treadmill belt. A replacement has to match your machine on loop length, width, seam and backing, and the listings worth buying are the ones that tell you all of that. Here are six that do, and how to check yours before you order.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
          <a href="#quick-picks" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
            See the Picks
          </a>
          <a href="#measure" class="bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm border border-white/20">
            How to Measure
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 py-8 border-b border-gray-100">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="48" height="48" class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full" />
        <div>
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight"><a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author" class="text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a></p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm leading-tight">Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block w-px h-8 bg-gray-200"></div>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
          Last Updated: <strong class="text-gray-700">November 6, 2026</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="1.2k" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose my-10 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 m-0 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-gray-900">On the products below.</strong> We have not tested these
          belts, and we have not fitted any of them to a treadmill. On 6 November 2026 we looked
          each one up on Amazon US and recorded the price shown and what the listing itself says
          about fit, size, seam and material. Every figure on a card comes from that listing; where
          a listing does not give a figure, the card does not either. Fit claims are the seller's,
          not ours, and this is a category dominated by small parts sellers rather than treadmill
          makers, so treat a model name in a title as a starting point and check it against your
          own machine's model number, serial number or measurements before ordering. Prices change
          often. We earn a commission if you buy through the Amazon links on this page; it does not
          change which products we list or what we say about them.
          <strong class="text-gray-900">Safety.</strong> Unplug the treadmill at the wall before
          you remove the motor hood or touch a roller, and if you are unsure about any step, a
          local treadmill technician is a better choice than guesswork.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>


    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-8">
